            // LHS went from (A || false) to (A || true), which is A to (A||true)
            // We need to check if this change is consistent with the equivalence

            // We have i >= pre_min, so from pre-invariant (condition was false):
            // (log_entry_is_alive(pre.alive_bits, i, pre.buffer_size) || false) <==> pre.contents.contains_key(i)
            // Which simplifies to: log_entry_is_alive(pre.alive_bits, i, pre.buffer_size) <==> pre.contents.contains_key(i)

            // In post-state (condition is true): 
            // (log_entry_is_alive(post.alive_bits, i, post.buffer_size) || true) <==> post.contents.contains_key(i)
            // Which simplifies to: true <==> post.contents.contains_key(i)
            // So: post.contents.contains_key(i) must be true

